## Goal
Address review feedback on the packaging and release work (DEV-75): make the build and release scripts more robust and improve the error hint in `portero default set`.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
- `scripts/build-app.sh`: the per-architecture binaries are collected in the positional parameters (`set --`) and passed to `lipo` and `rm` as quoted `"$@"`. This avoids unquoted word splitting if a path contains spaces.
- `scripts/package.sh` and `scripts/update-cask.sh`: file mode changed to executable (755) so they can be run directly.
- `scripts/update-cask.sh`: an empty tag is no longer accepted by the version pattern. It now fails with an explicit "empty tag" error.
- `cmd/portero/app.go`: when `default set` is run outside an app bundle, the error now shows the real path of the installed app if one is found (`installedApp()`). Otherwise it uses a generic `<Portero.app>` placeholder. It names both install locations: the brew cask in `/Applications` and `make install` in `~/Applications`. Previously it hardcoded one path.

